  general-litellm-adapter  [requested_behavior/explicit, code_and_tests]
     Every provider without a native adapter is served by a general adapter built on
     LiteLLM, so a run on such a provider completes without new code.
     look for: A run on a non-Anthropic provider, such as an OpenAI-style open-weight
     host, completes through the LiteLLM-backed adapter.
     < claim-03 (line 5): Its value is breadth — many providers behind one call — and
       that still matters: a user may be constrained to particular providers, and
       cheaper options such as open-weight models are worth measuring.
     < claim-16 (line 20): **A general adapter through LiteLLM** for every other
       provider, so a user's choice keeps working without new code.
     < claim-17 (line 20): Most open-weight hosts (vLLM, Ollama, Together, Fireworks)
       speak the OpenAI-style API, which LiteLLM covers.
     < claim-26 (line 35): A run on a provider with no native adapter completes through
       the general adapter.

